   "source": [
    "# Correlation between the numeric features and the target\n",
    "corr = df[list(colnum) + [target.name]].corr()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6, 5))\n",
    "sns.heatmap(corr, annot=True, fmt=\".3f\", cmap=\"RdBu_r\", center=0, vmin=-1, vmax=1,\n",
    "            square=True, linewidths=2, linecolor=\"white\", cbar_kws={\"shrink\": 0.75}, ax=ax)\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Correlation matrix\")\n",
    "fig.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "623b8329",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Deux informations dans cette matrice.**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Entre variables d'entrée, les corrélations sont nulles** (≈ 0,00). Elles sont indépendantes les unes des\n",
    "   autres — cohérent avec des tirages aléatoires séparés.\n",
    "2. **Face à la cible**, une seule variable ressort vraiment : `Rainfall_mm` (≈ 0,77). `Temperature_Celsius`\n",
    "   est à peine visible (≈ 0,08) et `Days_to_Harvest` est **à zéro**.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Conclusion 3 — la pluie explique l'essentiel du rendement ; la durée de culture n'explique rien.**\n",
    "\n",
    "Cette indépendance mutuelle a une conséquence directe sur l'ACP demandée par le brief. Vérifions-la."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 54,
   "id": "6f37eb34",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "explained variance ratio: [0.3342 0.3334 0.3324]\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 600x350 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "\n",
    "# PCA on the standardized numeric features: is there anything to compress?\n",
    "pca = PCA().fit(StandardScaler().fit_transform(df[colnum]))\n",
    "ratios = pca.explained_variance_ratio_\n",
    "print(\"explained variance ratio:\", ratios.round(4))\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6, 3.5))\n",
    "ax.bar(range(1, len(ratios) + 1), ratios * 100, color=BLUE, alpha=0.7, edgecolor=\"white\")\n",
    "ax.axhline(100 / len(ratios), color=INK, ls=\"--\", lw=1.5,\n",
    "           label=f\"{100 / len(ratios):.1f} % = strictly no compression\")\n",
    "ax.set_xticks(range(1, len(ratios) + 1))\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Principal component\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"% of variance explained\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Scree plot\")\n",
    "ax.legend(frameon=False)\n",
    "sns.despine(fig=fig)\n",
    "fig.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7d8ac188",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**L'ACP ne compresse rien — et c'est un résultat, pas un échec.**\n",
    "\n",
    "Les 3 composantes expliquent 33,4 % / 33,3 % / 33,2 % de la variance. Un scree plot parfaitement plat.\n",
    "\n",
    "L'ACP sert à regrouper des variables qui varient ensemble. Ici elles ont été tirées indépendamment, donc il\n",
    "n'y a **rien à regrouper**. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
